{"story_id":42960,"updated_at":"2026-10-24T18:15:20","headline_en":"Defending champion Shannon Tan trails Vani Kapoor by one stroke entering final","headline_hi":"डिफेंडिंग चैंपियन शैनन टैन फाइनल में प्रवेश करते समय वाणी कपूर से एक स्ट्रोक पीछे हैं।","payload_en":{"story_id":42960,"headline":"Defending champion Shannon Tan trails Vani Kapoor by one stroke entering final","counts":{"articles":2,"independent_sources":2,"outlets":2},"has_established":false,"qualified_by":"express","perspective_mode":"none","perspectives":{"–":["Hindustan Times","The Hindu"]},"framing":[],"suicide":false,"thread":42960,"parents":[],"children":[],"written_at":"2026-10-24T18:15:20","category":{"primary":["life"],"secondary":["sport-films"]},"places":[],"people":["Vani Kapoor","Pranavi Urs","Shannon Tan","Hero Women","Thai Pornanong Phatlum","Magdalena Simmermacher","Aditi Ashok","Argentina"],"narrative":{"paragraphs":[[{"text":"Vani Kapoor moved into a one-stroke lead during the third round after carding her second straight 3-under 69.","ids":[67673],"class":"partial","sources":[1,2]}],[{"text":"On Friday 23 October 2026, Shannon Tan found five birdies on the first six holes.","ids":[67663],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"On Saturday, the defending champion carded a five-under 67.","ids":[67674],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"On Saturday 24 October 2026, Chiara Tamburlini shot a 79 in the third round.","ids":[67661],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"On Saturday 24 October 2026, Kapoor topped the leaderboard at the Hero Women’s Indian Open after the third round.","ids":[67662],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"She took a one-shot lead into the final day of the Women’s Indian Open.","ids":[67678],"class":"single","sources":[1]},{"text":"The leader is seasoned Kapoor rather than Pranavi Urs, who recently won the Asian Games title.","ids":[67717,67718],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"On Saturday, Shannon Tan left for an appointment with the physio to be ready for Sunday.","ids":[67675],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Kapoor sunk three birdies on the front nine.","ids":[67707],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"She sunk two birdies on the back nine.","ids":[67708],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"Kapoor sunk a bogey on the 18th.","ids":[67709],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"Thai Pornanong Phatlum shot a 69 in the tournament.","ids":[67676],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Urs played an error-strewn round of 1-over par 73.","ids":[67677],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"In the second round, Kapoor holed out for an eagle.","ids":[67679],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Tan and Thai Pornanong Phatlum are tied second, one shot behind the leader.","ids":[67685],"class":"unverified","sources":[1,2]},{"text":"Urs is tied fourth with Argentina’s Magdalena Simmermacher.","ids":[67691],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Aditi Ashok is the only Indian to win the Hero Women’s Indian Open title as of 2016.","ids":[67666],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"Tvesa Malik was the only other Indian golfer under par, securing eighth place following a one-under 71.","ids":[67693],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"The race on Sunday is likely to be open.","ids":[67704],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"\"It's just another day for me to be honest, not that I've ever led an LET event, but I'm pretty calm and I just hope I stay this way,\" Kapoor said of hoping to stay that way for the final day, adding, \"It was one the most fun rounds that I've ever had. Of course, it was a little up and down towards the end, but I'm glad that I kept it together\" regarding being glad she kept it together towards the end of her round.","ids":[67715,67716,67680,67710],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Kapoor stated that she is calm.","ids":[67711],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Kapoor admitted she was not thinking too far ahead.","ids":[67668],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"Kapoor has a three-day total of 211.","ids":[67664],"class":"single","sources":[2]},{"text":"Round 3 top scores are: Kapoor 211; Shannon Tan and Pornanong Phatlum 212; Urs and Magdalena Simmermacher 213.","ids":[67670],"class":"single","sources":[2]}],[{"text":"The Hero Women’s Indian Open tournament has a prize fund of $500,000.","ids":[67681],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Following three rounds of play, just eight competitors remain under par in the competition.","ids":[67683],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Pornanong Phatlum was on 4-under for the tournament.","ids":[67690],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"Urs achieved five birdies across her opening six holes on the front nine.","ids":[67696],"class":"single","sources":[1]}],[{"text":"During the third round, Kapoor recorded four birdies within her first 11 holes.","ids":[67699],"class":"single","sources":[1]},{"text":"She had two bogeys and one birdie in the last four holes of the third round.","ids":[67700],"class":"single","sources":[1]}]],"section_keys":["news","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","happened","words","words","say","numbers","numbers","numbers","numbers","numbers","numbers"],"sources":[{"n":1,"url":"https://www.hindustantimes.com/sports/others/womens-indian-open-vani-kapoor-takes-one-shot-lead-into-final-day-101792858567327.html","outlet":"Hindustan Times","title":"Women’s Indian Open: Vani Kapoor takes one-shot lead into final day","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true},{"n":2,"url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/other-sports/hero-womens-indian-open-vani-in-the-van-for-the-first-time-ever-in-a-let-event/article71619981.ece","outlet":"The Hindu","title":"Hero Women’s Indian Open: Vani in the van for the first time ever in a LET event","perspective":"–","read":true,"readable":true}],"who":[null,null,null,null,nu