i Ashok is the only Indian to win the Hero Women’s Indian Open title as of 2016.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/other-sports/hero-womens-indian-open-vani-in-the-van-for-the-first-time-ever-in-a-let-event/article71619981.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Pranavi Urs and Magdalena Simmermacher are in the top five, one stroke behind the leaders.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/other-sports/hero-womens-indian-open-vani-in-the-van-for-the-first-time-ever-in-a-let-event/article71619981.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Vani Kapoor admitted she was not thinking too far ahead.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/other-sports/hero-womens-indian-open-vani-in-the-van-for-the-first-time-ever-in-a-let-event/article71619981.ece","stance":"attributes"}]},{"text":"Round 3 top scores are: Vani Kapoor 211; Shannon Tan and Pornanong Phatlum 212; Pranavi Urs and Magdalena Simmermacher 213.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/other-sports/hero-womens-indian-open-vani-in-the-van-for-the-first-time-ever-in-a-let-event/article71619981.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Vani Kapoor shot a second consecutive 3-under 69 in the third round to take a one-shot lead.","verdict":"unverified","n_sources":1,"sources":[{"outlet":"Hindustan Times","url":"https://www.hindustantimes.com/sports/others/womens-indian-open-vani-kapoor-takes-one-shot-lead-into-final-day-101792858567327.html","stance":"asserts"},{"outlet":"The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/sport/other-sports/hero-womens-indian-open-vani-in-the-van-for-the-first-time-ever-in-a-let-event/article71619981.ece","stance":"asserts"}]},{"text":"Singapore’s defending champion Shannon Tan carded a five-under 67 on Saturday.","verdict":"unverif